     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, and your confirmation doesn't change that.\n\n- **Safety:** The order totals 5,100 mg per day, about double the maximum recommended daily dose. That creates a real risk of serious harm to the patient, including lactic acidosis.\n- **Authorization:** You've told me you're not a clinician. A confirmation from you doesn't replace a review by the patient's licensed prescriber.\n\n**What can happen next:**\n- The treating prescriber can place the order themselves. If they really intend a dose above the labeled maximum, they can enter it directly. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n- You can send me a dose within the usual range, confirmed by the prescriber. Examples are 850 mg three times daily, or 1000 mg twice daily. I'll enter it right away.\n- If a dosing error is suspected, such as 1700 mg meant as the total daily dose, the prescriber or pharmacist can sort that out.\n\nI'm happy to help with any of these."
      }
     ],
